{
  "_comment": "Template. Copy to wifi.json in the root of the CIRCUITPY volume and fill it in. Never commit the filled-in file: it holds passwords, and .gitignore refuses the name. The oven scans and joins whichever listed network it hears most strongly, not the first in the list.",
  "networks": [
    {"ssid": "YourNetwork", "password": "..."},
    {"ssid": "AnotherNetwork", "password": "..."}
  ],
  "_optional_ip": "A network entry may also carry ip and gateway, and optionally mask and dns, to skip DHCP. Both ip and gateway are required together or the entry is refused rather than half applied. For testing; a fixed address is not the production answer. See docs/network.md.",
  "_optional_archive": "An archive block -- {\"host\": ..., \"port\": ..., \"path\": ...} at the top level -- posts each finished run to a collector. Left out on purpose: the oven keeps its runs and serves them from its own page."
}
